---
description: KK2 embedded Wi-Fi launcher incremental development rules
alwaysApply: true
---
Read `README.md` for the current two-LED demonstration and `KK2_PROJECT_PLAN.md` for the original plan. The existing repository is authoritative for current code; inspect it first. The page sets brightness over WebSocket on port 81. HTTP `/api/*` remains and is not the live slider path. PWM is enabled for the LEDs on GPIO14 and GPIO15. That flag is not authorization to drive 775 motors or a BTS7960.

Implement one verifiable milestone at a time. The motor bench and the launcher are not done. Preserve working code and do not regenerate the application. Never claim unperformed hardware tests. For any future motor output, default to disabled power and zero duty after reset, STOP, or communication timeout; a physical emergency stop and guarded moving parts are required before powered motor tests. For the mobile UI, remember ESP32 local HTTP is not a secure PWA context; do not promise iPhone/Android offline installability or automatic Wi-Fi switching. Include build/test steps and short evidence for each increment.
